From 54e5ee7228ed6810066be7f34429f723b8c85118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: papi <papi@papi-ux.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:56:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] feat(video): give the PyroWave refusal a code of its own

A client that asked for the codec and found no matching profile returned -1, which every
caller reads as a handshake that failed, and a handshake that failed sends someone to check
their firewall. This is not that: the codec was not on offer and the network is fine.

Proven live against a host without the codec, which now refuses with a reason about the
codec instead of a list of ports.
---
 src/Limelight.h      | 5 +++++
 src/RtspConnection.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Limelight.h b/src/Limelight.h
index eb3156f..28120bd 100644
--- a/src/Limelight.h
+++ b/src/Limelight.h
@@ -457,6 +457,11 @@ typedef void(*ConnListenerConnectionTerminated)(int errorCode);
 // supported on GFE 3.22+.
 #define ML_ERROR_FRAME_CONVERSION -104
 
+// The client asked for PyroWave and the host did not offer the exact profile it implements. Distinct
+// from a handshake that failed, because the two want opposite things from whoever reads them: this
+// one is a codec that was not on offer, and there is nothing wrong with the network.
+#define ML_ERROR_PYROWAVE_PROFILE_UNAVAILABLE -105
+
 // This callback is invoked to log debug message
 typedef void(*ConnListenerLogMessage)(const char* format, ...);
 
diff --git a/src/RtspConnection.c b/src/RtspConnection.c
index ce4d3d1..b3235b8 100644
--- a/src/RtspConnection.c
+++ b/src/RtspConnection.c
@@ -1154,7 +1154,7 @@ int performRtspHandshake(PSERVER_INFORMATION serverInfo) {
                 !sdpOffersPyroWaveProfile(response.payload)) {
                 Limelog("This host does not offer the PyroWave profile this client implements (%s)\n",
                         PYROWAVE_PROFILE_TOKEN);
-                ret = -1;
+                ret = ML_ERROR_PYROWAVE_PROFILE_UNAVAILABLE;
                 goto Exit;
             }
 
